  "result": "I found the cause of the odd `--help` ordering and have a fix planned, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is active. I also couldn't load the plan-approval tool, so I'm presenting the plan here.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names with `reverse=True`. That puts long names before short ones, so `--help` shows `--verbose, -v` instead of `-v, --verbose`. `Option.get_help_record` runs every option through this function. The other ordering code I checked (parameter order, the help option going last, commands sorted alphabetically) looks fine.\n\n**Planned change:**\n1. In `src/click/formatting.py:319`, change `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)` to `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])`. The sort is stable, so names with the same prefix length stay in declaration order.\n2. Fix any existing test expectations that encoded the old order, and add a regression test in `tests/test_formatting.py` asserting `join_options([\"--verbose\", \"-v\"])` returns `(\"-v, --verbose\", False)`.\n3. Run the full test suite and check `--help` output manually.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-functional-leaf.md`. Let me know if you'd like me to proceed with it.",
